Set the dot for the active buffer by writing a regular expression to the 'addr'
control file for that buffer in fsys.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/with-fsys.toml
-- file-hello.txt --
hello, world!
-- actions --
fsys: write buffers/1/addr /world.*$/
-- buffer-list --
1    * hello.txt
-- expected-windows --
1
-- expected-buffer-1 --
hello, world!

-- expected-buffer-dot-1 --
world!
